                      "blocks": {
                        "accordion_row_HNtkxm": {
                          "type": "_accordion-row",
                          "settings": {
                            "heading": "Will the Giant Grill Gauge fit my grill?",
                            "open_by_default": false,
                            "icon": "none",
                            "width": 20
                          },
                          "blocks": {
                            "text_84hCYd": {
                              "type": "text",
                              "settings": {
                                "text": "<p>The Gauge replaces the existing dial thermometer on many grills and smokers. Check the mounting area before choosing a mount:</p><ul><li>Thermometer hole: 5/32–1/4 in</li><li>Flat mounting area: 4.3 in (109 mm) across</li><li>Clearance around the mounting point: 2.5 in (64 mm)</li></ul><p><strong>Heat Shield:</strong> for top-mounted thermometers or hotter lids, up to 750°F (399°C). <strong>Heat Deflector:</strong> for front or side mounting, up to 600°F (316°C).</p><p>Some ceramic grills need an adapter plate, and thick walls may need a longer sensor than the Gauge’s 86 mm tube. If your grill needs an adapter or does not meet these measurements, email <a href=\"mailto:support@combustion.inc\" target=\"_blank\">support@combustion.inc</a> with your grill’s make, model and a photo to confirm the fit before ordering.</p>",
                                "width": "fit-content",
                                "max_width": "none",
                                "alignment": "left",
                                "type_preset": "custom",
                                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                                "font_size": "1rem",
                                "line_height": "normal",
                                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                                "case": "none",
                                "wrap": "pretty",
